  "source-window": "$\\yoneda:X\\to\\hat{X}$ is fully faithful.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\subsection{L-separation}\\label{LsepV}\nFor $\\V$-functors $f,g:Z\\to X$ we write $f\\cong g$ if $f\\le g$ and $g\\le f$; equivalently, if $f^*=g^*$, or $f_*=g_*$. We call $X$ \\emph{L-separated} if $f\\cong g$ implies $f=g$, for all $f,g:Z\\to X$. The full subcategory of $\\Cat{\\V}$ consisting of all L-separated $\\V$-categories is denoted by $\\CatSep{\\V}$. Obviously, it suffices to consider $Z=E$ (the $\\otimes$-neutral object) here: writing $x:E\\to X$ in $\\Cat{\\V}$ instead of $x\\in X$, we just note that $f_*=g_*$ implies\n\\[\n(f\\cdot x)_*=f_*\\cdot x_*=g_*\\cdot x_*=(g\\cdot x)_*.\n\\]\nThis proves the equivalence of (i),(ii) of the following proposition.\n",
